# Doji monorepo: env files live per app (no root .env).
#
# Copy and fill from:
#   apps/server/.env.example  →  apps/server/.env
#   apps/web/.env.example     →  apps/web/.env   (or .env.local)
#
# Server (apps/server/.env): MAGIC_SECRET_KEY, CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY,
#   JWT_SESSION_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, PORT, CORS_ORIGIN, POLYMARKET_BUILDER_*,
#   POLYMARKET_SIGN_TOKENS (prod), POLYGON_RPC_URL, SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT.
#   API URLs (GAMMA/DATA/BRIDGE/CLOB) and CHAIN_ID have defaults — set only to override.
#
# Web (apps/web/.env or .env.local): NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL,
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MAGIC_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, NEXT_PUBLIC_POLYGON_RPC_URL,
#   POLYMARKET_SIGN_TOKEN, SENTRY_DEBUG, SENTRY_RELEASE, SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN,
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DEBUG, SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT.
#   WS/CLOB/RTDS URLs and CHAIN_ID have defaults — set only to override.
#
# Sentry: Both apps use SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT to tag events per deployment target.
#   Set explicitly in Vercel (not NODE_ENV fallback):
#     Production: "production", Preview: "staging", Development: "development"
#
# Note: @doji/api tests load apps/server/.env via vitest.config (same as server app).
